    "created_at": "2017-10-26T06:00:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-26T06:00:20Z",
    "body": "Hi @jernoble —  That can work in some cases. However one major issue there is that pitch and speed are coupled. The problem from the user's perspective is that the user cannot independently adjust pitch and speed. \r\n\r\nA lot of music needs pitch adjustment to be in standard tuning. Old Van Halen, for example, is about 80 cents flat of standard tuning. The user should be able to bring it up to pitch and then slow it down. But that's not possible with preservesPitch because pitch is coupled to playbackRate. \r\n\r\nIf you try the bookmarklet i made, you'll see what I mean. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
